{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373564-tiger-style-warrior-training-technique","id":1373564,"title":"Tiger (Style) Warrior Training Technique","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-08T10:02:31-07:00","id":1373564,"title":"Tiger (Style) Warrior Training Technique","content":"So I hope this isn't too self-indulgent, but I thought this would merit its own thread. Maybe I'm wrong &amp; it'll fade into obscurity. It's a tangent from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?_=1583684984259\">this thread</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373189#post1373189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I'm thinking of putting together a custom charm enhancing Tiger Warrior Training Technique to help him do that. Something that allows elite martial artists to be trained, and probably offers some training in complementary abilities. It might be cool to come up with an extra add-on for each style (comparable to Demon-Fighting Principle, Giant-Slaying Tactics etc) that gives some unique benefit, but there are so many styles. Still, maybe I can just come up with ideas that that character might use and then crowdsource the rest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my first draft: <b>Efficacious Solar Sifu:<br /> Cost:</b> - <b>Mins:</b> War 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Tiger Warrior Training Technique, one Martial Arts form charm<br /> <br /> This charm enhances the Solar's Tiger Warrior Training Technique. It confers the Martial Artist Merit on the Tiger Warriors being trained and allows them to be trained in a Martial Art known by the instructing Solar instead of another combat ability. Tiger Warriors trained to a competent level with this charm can use a dice pool of 5 dice for pools based on their style's complementary abilities. If trained to an elite level, they can use a pool of 9 dice instead.<br /> <br /> Further enhancements become available at Essence 3+ depending on the style being taught:<br /> <b>False Friend Inception </b>(Ebon Shadow Style) (2xp): Generals commanding units of Ebon Shadow Stylists gain access to an enhanced Ambush stratagem in the Strategic Maneuver roll-off. In addition to the usual effects, a significant number of enemy troops turn out to be Ebon Shadow infiltrators who open the battle by stabbing their \u201ccomrades\u201d in the back, provoking an immediate rout check. If this rout check is passed, the enemy commander suffers a +2 difficulty penalty to command actions for the remainder of the battle owing to the resulting confusion and disarray.<br /> <b>Poisonous Courtier Ideology</b> (Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style) (2xp): An army of Dreaming Pearl Courtesans is as useful in politics as in war. They can be deployed to embed themselves among high society, courtesans, street performers etc. where they can gather information or simply wait for the right moment to strike. The Courtesan army may even be smuggled in numbers into environments where weapons must ordinarily be left behind or peace-bound.<br /> <br /> ===<br /> <br /> It's late and I don't have the best head for mechanics, so maybe there are glaring balance oversights in this. If people have refinements I'm open to them. But I'm really interested in people's ideas for enhancements that Tiger Warriors might get through other martial arts styles. I didn't really try to develop strictly combat-focused ones like you might get from Tiger Style or Snake Style. How would you even differentiate between a Golden Janissary one and the canon Demon-Fighting Principle? These are questions I'd love to hear other people's ideas about.<br /> <br /> The 5/9 complementary ability pool is based on other pools that regular troops/elite troops get on page 497. Regular troops get 4 dice for Senses and Threaten, but that felt too low to me.<br /> <br /> I think the Ebon Shadow Style one could be really fun in the mirror match, where the generals vie to see whose plants will be in position to strike.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T10:43:47-07:00","id":1373569,"title":"","content":"How about...<br /> <br /> <b>Pouncing Tiger Onslaught</b> (Tiger Style) (2xp): When a unit of Tiger Stylists, following a command action by their sifu-general, moves a range band before attacking, they enjoy double 10s on their damage roll.<br /> <br /> I inserted the command action requirement because I wasn't sure about the balance, but maybe it isn't necessary. Is it inappropriate to require that the command action be given by the specific Solar who trained them? (Not really sure it makes sense, but I also really like the term &quot;sifu-general&quot; for some reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T10:54:09-07:00","id":1373572,"title":"","content":"<b>Crippling Serpent Fangs</b> (Snake Style) (2xp): When a unit of Snake Stylists, following a command action by their sifu-general, attacks and successfully deals damage, any victims damages suffer a -2 penalty on all actions on their next turn. Individual fighters who took <i>only</i> withering damage from the attack may resist this penalty by rolling (Stamina+Resistance) against a difficulty of (unit's Size+sifu-general's Essence).<br /> <br /> Not sure how to balance this one but it's meant to represent the Snake dudes all throwing whatever variant of Crippling Pressure-Point Strike they can as they move in.<br /> <br /> <b>Whirling Reaper Squadron </b>(White Reaper Style) (2xp): A unit of White Reaper Stylists always damages enemy battle groups with double 10s and enjoys +1 Defense against them.<br /> <br /> This...isn't really fair at all, but White Reaper is meant to be comically unfair <i>against</i>battle groups, so if you send your army against an army of <i>them</i> you might just deserve this. I dunno, too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T11:31:14-07:00","id":1373578,"title":"","content":"<b>Thousand-Leg Embrace</b> (Centipede Style) (2xp): A unit of Centipede Stylists gains +2 on control rolls while taking the engage action, as well as while opposing the engage actions of others.<br /> <br /> <b>Dual Venoms Prana </b>(Snake + Centipede Style) (3xp, requires Crippling Serpent Fangs and Thousand-Leg Embrace): When following a command action by their sifu-general to attack, the sifu-general may reflexively spend 5m for the stylists' attack to deliver the effect of Venom-Dripping Mandible (effect based on the sifu-general's Essence) to any victim taking damage. Battle groups cannot roll to reduce duration, but individual targets who take only withering damage gain +2 to their roll to reduce duration.<br /> <br /> ...This one might not have been a good idea, but I had an idea and needed to write it out. Of course, it does have pretty serious prerequisites overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T18:51:37-07:00","id":1373653,"title":"","content":"<b>Camaraderie-Severing Strikes</b> (Laughing Monster Style) (2xp): When a battlegroup of Laughing Monster Stylists reduces an enemy battlegroup's magnitude to 0, reduce the drill by 1 as the enemy soldiers lose cohesion and respect for each other. If they are already at poor drill, increase the difficulty of the roll to avoid rout by 1.<br /> <br /> Probably should do something to non-battlegroups, but I'm not sure what.<br /> <br /> <b>Ally-Protecting Kata </b>(Crane Style) (2xp): If a battlegroup of Crane stylists takes a full defense action, until their next turn they may respond to any attack against them with a <b>withering</b> counterattacks. If they take a defend other action, they may defend any number of allies in close range, and may respond to all attacks against their ward with a counterattack. These attacks are single target, but gain all other benefits of being a battlegroup. If commanded to take a full defense action or defend other action, the bonus dice apply to all attacks made under this benefit<br /> <br /> Is basically just crane form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T20:12:33-07:00","id":1373661,"title":"","content":"Are these comparable to the +2 might or unbreakable morale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T21:58:09-07:00","id":1373688,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not the best person to ask about balance. I was mostly trying to come up with minor, thematic, and interesting bonuses.<br /> <br /> Unrelatedly: I just noticed that Crane Style has Performance, Presence, <i>and</i> Socialize as complementary skills. A Crane sifu actually trains better socialites than even the DPC sifu...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:22:55-07:00","id":1373739,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, you're right. But surely that would be abstracted away by the fact that NPCs are just rolling &quot;Carouse: (9 dice)&quot; or what-have-you. Their actions aren't going to be so important that we need to care whether they're rolling Presence or Socialise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T12:31:13-07:00","id":1373800,"title":"","content":"True. It was a funny thought, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T14:08:56-07:00","id":1373812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373564-tiger-style-warrior-training-technique?p=1373739#post1373739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow, you're right. But surely that would be abstracted away by the fact that NPCs are just rolling &quot;Carouse: (9 dice)&quot; or what-have-you. Their actions aren't going to be so important that we need to care whether they're rolling Presence or Socialise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if it had been <i>just </i>Presence, their Guile would be lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T00:08:04-07:00","id":1374075,"title":"","content":"HUH. Now you mention it, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style doesn't actually use socialise, so their Guile will be lower. I'll probably just fudge that if someone tries it. It doesn't seem right for the Dreaming Pearl army to lack Guile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}